**nitpick**: This is better from a TypeScript perspective.

```suggestion
      const textElement = shapeSvg.select<SVGTextElement>('.label text');
      const textNode = textElement.node();
```

Not a big issue since we don't seem to have any CSS for `title-row`, but this should be the following:

```suggestion
      select(svgLabel).selectAll('tspan.text-outer-tspan').classed('title-row', true);
    } else {
      select(svgLabel).selectAll('tspan.text-outer-tspan').classed('row', true);
```

It sounds like `selection.classed(names, true)` is better, since it won't delete any existing classes on the `<tspan>`, unlike `.attr('class', names)`. See https://d3js.org/d3-selection/modifying#selection_classed
